    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n92588" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥόδῐνος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">η</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥόδον</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>made of</i> or <i>from
				roses</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στέφανος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Anacr.
					83
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄλειφα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hippon.
					58
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύρον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Cephisod.
					3
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μύρον</span> is understood in
				<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>Od.</u>
				25
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				<u>PPetr.</u>
				2p.114
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.43
			</span></i>; sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔλαιον</span>,
				<i>Edict.Diocl.</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Delph.
				6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				1172.8
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Lebena</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
